# Research evaluation

Follow `BACKEND_EVALUATION_RULES.md`.

Hard rules:

- The LLM extracts structured facts only (purpose, conditions, industrial use, transfer need, evidence counts).
- Assign `category`, `confidence`, `applicability`, and evidence quality via `src/lib/research` — never by asking the model “Established / Adjacent / Exploratory?”.
- Do not invent parallel classification in UI or prompts.
- Reuse `@/types`; retain classification inputs (e.g. `classificationEvidence`) alongside outputs.
- Validate LLM output with schemas before applying rules.
